# keys.pdl - what each GAMEKEY name of rmmc-pchq/pieces/system/keybinds.pdl DOES: one verb page (CONFIG; rmmc_driver holds no verb of its own).
# KEYVERB | gamekey name | verb | arg
KEYVERB | left  | walk | w
KEYVERB | right | walk | e
KEYVERB | up    | walk | n
KEYVERB | down  | walk | s
KEYVERB | jump  | jump | -
KEYVERB | mine  | mine | -
KEYVERB | place | place | -
# RULE rows: poll_ms = how often the driver looks at the relay file; idle_after_ms = how long after the last key the pose goes back to idle (the ledger has no clock, so the DRIVER owns the expiry: it re-projects with --idle)
RULE | poll_ms | 100
RULE | idle_after_ms | 400
